  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "GSearch 2.2 works with axis1. Investigate if we can/should upgrade to axis2 ( ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://axis.apache.org/axis2/java/core/"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://axis.apache.org/axis2/java/core/",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " )",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "From: \tAlistair Young <alistair.young@uhi.ac.uk>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Subject: \t[fcrepo-user] gsearch 2.2 wsdl breaks with axis2",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Date: \t7. aug 2011 17.58.29 CEST",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "To: \tSupport and info exchange list for Fedora users. <fedora-commons-users@lists.sourceforge.net>",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Does anyone know if there's a fix or workaround for the gsearch wsdl? Running axis2 + xmlbeans over it gives this error:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "org.apache.xmlbeans.XmlException: error: cvc-identity-constraint.4.2.2: Duplicate key 'gfindObjects' for key constraint 'element@",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema'"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema'",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "running the same config over Fedora API-A and API-M works fine.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
