  "description": "<p>GSearch 2.2 works with axis1. Investigate if we can/should upgrade to axis2 ( <a href=\"http://axis.apache.org/axis2/java/core/\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://axis.apache.org/axis2/java/core/</a> )</p>\n\n<p>\tFrom: \tAlistair Young &lt;alistair.young@uhi.ac.uk&gt;<br/>\n\tSubject: \t<span class=\"error\">&#91;fcrepo-user&#93;</span> gsearch 2.2 wsdl breaks with axis2<br/>\n\tDate: \t7. aug 2011 17.58.29 CEST<br/>\n\tTo: \tSupport and info exchange list for Fedora users. &lt;fedora-commons-users@lists.sourceforge.net&gt;</p>\n\n\n<p>Does anyone know if there's a fix or workaround for the gsearch wsdl? Running axis2 + xmlbeans over it gives this error:</p>\n\n<p>org.apache.xmlbeans.XmlException: error: cvc-identity-constraint.4.2.2: Duplicate key 'gfindObjects' for key constraint 'element@<a href=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema</a>'</p>\n\n<p>running the same config over Fedora API-A and API-M works fine.</p>",
